	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Keyword: repo

Finds git repos under REPO_ROOTS (colon-separated, default ~/Projects:~/Developer) down to REPO_DEPTH levels (default 4). Does not descend into repos; skips node_modules, vendor, .venv, venv, dist, build and dot-directories. Index cached for 5 minutes in the workflow cache; a query with no hits rescans at once.

Subtitle: path · branch (or short SHA when detached; worktrees followed) · IDE.
IDE from top-level files, first match wins: .sln/.csproj/.fsproj rider, composer.json phpstorm, go.mod goland, Cargo.toml rustrover, pyproject.toml/setup.py/requirements.txt pycharm, package.json/deno.json webstorm, else IDE_DEFAULT (default phpstorm). Launchers in /usr/local/bin. ↩ reads the app binary from the Toolbox launcher and runs open -na &lt;binary&gt; --args &lt;path&gt; (the launcher breaks paths with spaces); falls back to the launcher, then to open &lt;path&gt;.

↩  open in detected IDE
⌘↩ open in Fork
⌥↩ terminal at the repo (Alfred's Terminal setting)
⌃↩ terminal + CLAUDE_CMD (default claude) in the repo
⇧↩ reveal in Finder
⌘C copy path

Tests: /usr/bin/python3 -B -m unittest test_repo</string>
